  "id": "charles-bonnet-syndrome",
  "term": "Charles Bonnet syndrome",
  "definition": "Charles Bonnet syndrome is a condition in which a person, most often an older adult with reduced vision or visual field loss, repeatedly sees things that are not really there. They typically recognize that these visual experiences are unreal, and the syndrome is not linked to delusions or hallucinations in other senses.",
